script.gvcv5.battleInfo0.name=When an entity is hit by a projectile, the projectile's penetration value is first compared to the entity's armor value; damage is dealt only if the penetration value is equal to or greater than the armor value.
script.gvcv5.battleInfo1.name=§6 Penetration Value§r is a value that represents the ability of projectiles, such as artillery shells and rocket-propelled grenades, to penetrate armor, while §b Armor Value§r is a value that represents the thickness of a vehicle's armor.
script.gvcv5.battleInfo2.name=If the penetration value exceeds the armor value, the amount of damage is determined by “weapon power × (1 - damage reduction rate).”
script.gvcv5.battleInfo3.name=The damage reduction rate varies depending on the armor and the body part hit.
script.gvcv5.battleInfo4.name=You can reduce bullet damage by equipping armor on four body parts: the head, chest, legs, and feet. The bullet damage reduction rate provided by armor for each body part is as follows. The reduction rate remains the same regardless of which body part the armor is equipped on.
script.gvcv5.battleInfo5.name=§2 Hides, Ghillie Suits: 5% per body part§r
script.gvcv5.battleInfo6.name=§6 Chain Armor: 10% per slot§r
script.gvcv5.battleInfo7.name=§7 Iron Armor: 15% per piece§r
script.gvcv5.battleInfo8.name=§fPlastic Gear: 20% per slot§r
script.gvcv5.battleInfo9.name=§9 Diamond Gear: 22.5% per slot§r
script.gvcv5.battleInfo10.name=§8 Netherite Armor: 25% per piece§r
script.gvcv5:battleInfo11.name=The damage reduction rate for armor can reach a maximum of 100% when all four pieces are equipped.
script.gvcv5:battleInfo12.name=Additionally, if you take a §cHeadshot§r, the damage reduction rate is reduced by 50%. Furthermore, if you are hit in the legs, the damage reduction rate is increased by 25%.
script.gvcv5:battleInfo13.name=If the damage reduction rate falls below 0%, the damage taken increases.

